                <pb facs="0290" n="218" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg218"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 28 in No. 331.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Daly to Mr.
                            Tinsley, consular agent at
                    Limerick.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Limerick County Jail</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Friday</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1881-10-28"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 28,
                    1881</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I beg to inform you that I, James F. Daly,
                    a citizen of the United States, have been arrested by the lord lieutenant’s
                    warrant and detained here at his will on a charge which “I challenge him to
                    prove against me.” Will you be so kind as to come and see me as quickly as
                    possible, and forward my naturalization papers to the American minister to
                    demand for me a trial or speedy release.</p>
                <p>I beg to remain, yours, respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed>JAMES F. DALY.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
